---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Master Said to Me — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 105"
  description="Chullin 105: survive one Babylonian evening meal. Patrol your fields, wash the right waters the right way, wait out the cheese after meat, guard the crumbs from the angel of poverty, sink the foam, dodge the witchcraft in a tied bundle, and keep your barrel out from under the gutter — while Abaye keeps discovering that every table habit he thought was mere manners is really about demons, blindness, and the evil spirit."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#140e08] !text-[#ecdfc6]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#3d2c1a] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#241809]/90 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#e6a94f]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#f5c97e]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 105 · 2026-08-27
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">🕯️ The Master Said to Me</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-xl !text-[#e6a94f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מֵרֵישׁ הֲוָה אָמֵינָא… אָמַר לִי מָר</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-1 text-xs italic !text-[#a78d68]">"At first I would say… but the Master said to me" — Abaye's refrain, eight times on Chullin 105b</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cbb894]">
        On this daf, dinner is dangerous. Eight times Abaye admits he thought a table custom was
        just manners — and eight times his teacher Rabba reveals the hidden reason: an evil spirit
        on the spilled water, an angel of poverty hunting your crumbs, witchcraft in a knotted
        bundle of greens, a demon dozing under the gutter. Play one evening in a Babylonian
        household, from the dusk patrol of your fields to the last drink from the pitcher. Every
        choice is judged by the daf itself.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Meters ============ -->
      <div class="sticky top-2 z-20 mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#1e1610]/95 p-3 shadow-lg shadow-black/40 backdrop-blur">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-center" id="meters"></div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-center text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#a78d68]">
          the master's reasons learned: <span id="master-count" class="font-bold !text-[#e6a94f]">0</span> / 8
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Game ============ -->
      <div id="game"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#1e1610] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#e6a94f]">learn the real daf</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#cbb894]">
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">Wipe and rinse.</b> The Gemara resolves Beit Shammai and Beit Hillel: after meat one must
            both wipe the mouth and rinse it — the two houses were never arguing. Rabbi Zeira: wiping works only with bread,
            and only cold, soft wheat bread; the halakha concludes anything wipes except flour, dates, and vegetables
            (<a class="!text-[#e6a94f] underline hover:!text-[#f5c97e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">105a:1–5</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">Meat, then cheese.</b> Rabbi Yoḥanan: cheese before meat needs no wait at all. Rav Ḥisda:
            meat before cheese is forbidden immediately — and "while the meat was yet between their teeth" (Numbers 11:33) proves
            meat stuck in the teeth still counts. Mar Ukva calls himself "vinegar, son of wine": his father waited a full day; he
            waits only until the next meal
            (<a class="!text-[#e6a94f] underline hover:!text-[#f5c97e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">105a:6–9</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">Patrol your property.</b> Shmuel: patrol daily and you'll find an asteira coin. Abaye catches
            his sharecropper mid-theft; Rav Asi, grumbling that the coins never appear, plugs a burst water channel with his own
            cloak — "I have found all the asteira coins"
            (<a class="!text-[#e6a94f] underline hover:!text-[#f5c97e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">105a:10–12</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">Three waters.</b> First waters are a rabbinic mitzva — vessel or ground, hot or cold. Middle
            waters are optional between dishes but obligatory between a dish and cheese (Rav Naḥman). Final waters are an
            obligation — because of Sodomite salt, a pinch per kor, which blinds the eye — cold only, and into a vessel
            (<a class="!text-[#e6a94f] underline hover:!text-[#f5c97e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">105a:13–105b:5</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">Abaye's eight revisions.</b> Ground-spilled final waters, snatching from the table while a
            cup is raised, scattered crumbs, drinking the foam, tied bundles, fallen vegetables, sitting under the gutter, the
            first splash from the pitcher — each mundane habit hides an unseen hazard, capped by the poverty-angel driven out with
            a hoe and the demon who pays for a burst barrel
            (<a class="!text-[#e6a94f] underline hover:!text-[#f5c97e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">105b:5–19</a>).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#e6a94f]/40 bg-[#e6a94f]/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#e6a94f] hover:bg-[#e6a94f]/20">Chullin 105 on Sefaria →</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.105a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#3d2c1a] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a78d68] hover:!text-[#ecdfc6]">Rashi (×81)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Chullin.105a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#3d2c1a] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a78d68] hover:!text-[#ecdfc6]">Rabbeinu Gershom (×41)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.105a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#3d2c1a] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a78d68] hover:!text-[#ecdfc6]">Steinsaltz (×36)</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 text-center text-[10px] !text-[#7a6749]">
        <a href="/daf" class="underline hover:!text-[#e6a94f]">← back to the daf yomi arcade</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    [lang='he'] { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .flip-wrap { perspective: 900px; }
    .flip-inner {
      position: relative;
      transform-style: preserve-3d;
      transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
    }
    .flip-wrap.flipped .flip-inner { transform: rotateX(180deg); }
    .flip-face {
      backface-visibility: hidden;
      -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
    }
    .flip-back {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      transform: rotateX(180deg);
      overflow-y: auto;
    }
    .pip { transition: opacity 0.4s ease, transform 0.4s ease; }
    .pip.lost { opacity: 0.15; transform: scale(0.7); }
    .scene-enter { animation: sceneIn 0.45s ease both; }
    @keyframes sceneIn {
      from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
      to { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .flip-inner { transition: none; }
      .scene-enter { animation: none; }
      .pip { transition: none; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    // ---------- state ----------
    const METERS = [
      { key: 'body', label: 'guf · body', he: 'גּוּף', icon: '🫀', color: '#d4674c' },
      { key: 'purse', label: 'mamon · purse', he: 'מָמוֹן', icon: '🪙', color: '#d9b23f' },
      { key: 'spirit', label: 'ruach · spirit', he: 'רוּחַ', icon: '🕯️', color: '#a893d1' },
    ];
    let state;
    function freshState() {
      return { scene: 0, body: 3, purse: 3, spirit: 3, chasidut: 0, masterSeen: new Set(), log: [] };
    }

    // ---------- the evening, scene by scene, straight from the daf ----------
    // outcome.meter: which meter takes the hit (null = no hit). outcome.tone: 'good' | 'bad' | 'warn' | 'machloket'
    const SCENES = [
      {
        kicker: 'dusk · before the meal',
        title: 'Walk the fields, or sit down to eat?',
        he: 'הֲוָה סָיַיר נִכְסֵיהּ כׇּל יוֹמָא',
        body: 'The table is nearly set. Shmuel taught: one who patrols his property every day will find an asteira coin. Abaye patrolled daily; Rav Asi patrolled and grumbled that the coins never appeared.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105a:10–12',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.10',
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Patrol the fields one last time before dark',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'You find Shmuel’s asteira.', text: 'Out by the irrigation channel the water has burst its banks and is flooding your field. Like Rav Asi, you stuff your wrapped cloak into the breach, cry out, and neighbors come seal it. "I have just found all the asteira coins mentioned by Mar Shmuel" (105a:12).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'The stew is hot — stay inside',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'purse', title: 'A load of wood walks away.', text: 'Your sharecropper shoulders a load of your wood and heads home with it. When Abaye patrolled daily he caught his sharecropper in exactly this act: "The Sages already preempted you" (105a:11). Nobody preempted yours.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'first waters · mayim rishonim',
        title: 'The bread is before you. How do you wash?',
        he: 'מַיִם רִאשׁוֹנִים מִצְוָה',
        body: 'Rav Idi bar Avin said in the name of Rav Yitzḥak bar Ashyan: the first waters, before bread, are a mitzva by rabbinic law. The baraita rules how they may be poured.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105a:13–16',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.13',
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Pour cold water over your hands into a basin',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Washed.', text: 'For first waters one may pour into a vessel or onto the ground, hot or cold — a vessel is beyond question (105a:15, 17).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Pour it over your hands straight onto the ground',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Also fine — for these waters.', text: 'The baraita permits first waters "either into a vessel or onto the ground" (105a:15). Remember that this leniency is for the first waters only. The final waters will be another matter.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Use water so hot your hand recoils from it',
            outcome: { tone: 'machloket', meter: null, title: 'That depends which version you learned.', text: 'Rabbi Yannai’s ruling comes down in two versions: in the first, water the hand recoils from is barred even for first waters (105a:17–105b:1); in the second, first waters are valid even then (105b:2). You washed into a machloket.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Skip it — your hands look clean',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'spirit', title: 'You skipped a mitzva.', text: 'First waters are a mitzva by rabbinic law (105a:13). Clean-looking hands were never the point.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'the meat course',
        title: 'The meat is finished — and there is cheese in the house.',
        he: 'אֲכַל בִּשְׂרָא אֲסוּר לְמֵיכַל גְּבִינָה',
        body: 'Rav Ḥisda: one who ate meat may not eat cheese right away — though cheese before meat needs no wait at all, as Rabbi Yoḥanan told Rav Asi. And Rav Ḥisda answered Rav Aḥa bar Yosef with a verse: "while the meat was yet between their teeth" (Numbers 11:33) — meat in the teeth is still meat.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105a:6–9',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.6',
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Bring out the cheese now',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'spirit', title: 'The meat is yet between your teeth.', text: 'Rav Ḥisda forbids cheese immediately after meat (105a:7), and the verse he cited to Rav Aḥa bar Yosef says the shreds in your teeth still count as meat (105a:8).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'No cheese until a different meal',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'You keep Mar Ukva’s own practice.', text: '"At this meal, during which I ate meat, I do not eat cheese; at a different meal I will" — Mar Ukva’s standard, which he himself called vinegar, son of wine, next to his father’s (105a:9).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'No cheese until tomorrow at this hour',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, chasidut: true, title: 'You keep his father’s practice — wine, son of wine.', text: 'Mar Ukva’s father, having eaten meat, would not touch cheese until the same hour the next day (105a:9). The stricter path of the two, and you took it.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'wiping and rinsing',
        title: 'Clean the meat from your mouth. With what?',
        he: 'אֵין קִינּוּחַ הַפֶּה אֶלָּא בְּפַת',
        body: 'The Gemara resolves Beit Shammai and Beit Hillel: after meat one wipes the mouth and rinses it — both, and no one disagrees. Rabbi Zeira taught what wiping takes; the halakha closes the list.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105a:1–5',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105a.1',
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Cold, soft wheat bread — then rinse with water',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Exactly Rabbi Zeira’s bread.', text: 'Wheat, not barley (it crumbles); cold, not warm (it sticks to the palate); soft, not hard (it doesn’t clean). You wiped with the one bread that passes every test, and rinsed as the resolved dispute requires (105a:3–5).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'A piece of warm barley bread',
            outcome: { tone: 'warn', meter: null, title: 'The halakha lets it pass. Rabbi Zeira would not.', text: 'Barley crumbles in the mouth and warm bread clings to the palate — Rabbi Zeira disqualifies both for wiping (105a:4–5). The closing halakha is broader — all items wipe except three — but you did not choose well.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'A handful of dates',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'spirit', title: 'Dates are on the forbidden list.', text: 'The halakha concludes: everything constitutes effective wiping except flour, dates, and vegetables (105a:5). The taste of meat rides with you toward the cheese course.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'at the table',
        title: 'Your guest raises his cup. You want the spice mortar in front of him.',
        he: 'אֵין נוֹטְלִין מִן הַשֻּׁלְחָן כְּשֶׁאָדָם אוֹחֵז כּוֹס',
        body: 'The Sages said not to take things from the table while a person is holding a cup to drink. The daf spells out the limits — and Mar bar Rav Ashi would not remove even the mortar and pestle.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:6–8',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.6',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Not taking from the table while someone holds a cup', first: 'lest a mishap occur — unable to speak, he might choke in his anger', master: 'it is bad for his health: a spirit of pain in half the head — a migraine', ref: '105b:6' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Carry the mortar off to the far end of the house',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'A spirit of pain in half the head.', text: 'You took an item needed for the meal, beyond four cubits, and did not return it — all three conditions that make it forbidden (105b:7). Your guest sets down his cup and presses his temple.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Grind your spices and set the mortar straight back',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Taken and returned — no harm.', text: '"Taking and putting back, we have no problem with it" (105b:7). Within the limits the Sages drew.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Wait for him to set the cup down',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, chasidut: true, title: 'The care of Mar bar Rav Ashi.', text: 'Mar bar Rav Ashi was particular not to remove anything — even the mortar and pestle for spices (105b:8). You matched him.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'after the bread',
        title: 'Crumbs lie scattered across the table and floor.',
        he: 'מְכַנְּשִׁי נִשְׁוַורָאֵי',
        body: 'People collect the crumbs of bread after a meal. Abaye thought he knew why. Elsewhere in this daf, a certain man was hunted for years by the ministering angel of poverty — and never caught, because of his crumbs.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:9–10',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.9',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Collecting the crumbs after a meal', first: 'it is a matter of cleanliness', master: 'leaving them is bad for a person — it invites poverty', ref: '105b:9' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Gather every crumb',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'The angel of poverty groans.', text: 'The man in the daf was so careful with crumbs the angel could never impoverish him. When crumbs finally fell into the grass, he uprooted the grass with a hoe and threw it in the river — and heard the angel wail: "that man has removed me from my house" (105b:10).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Leave them for the morning sweep',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'purse', title: 'Something takes up residence.', text: 'Leaving crumbs is bad for a person’s vulnerability to poverty (105b:9). In the corner of the room, something patient settles in to wait.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'the drink',
        title: 'Your beer arrives wearing a cap of foam.',
        he: 'לָא שָׁתֵי אוּפְיָא',
        body: 'People do not drink the foam from the top of a beverage. The daf prices out every way of dealing with it — drinking it, blowing it, skimming it — and leaves exactly one safe move.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:11–12',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.11',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Not drinking the foam off the top', first: 'it is repulsive', master: 'it is bad for catarrh — and beer treats wine’s catarrh, water treats beer’s, and water’s has no remedy: poverty follows the poor', ref: '105b:11–12' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Drink it, foam and all',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'Catarrh.', text: 'Drinking the foam is bad for catarrh (105b:11). The remedy for beer-foam catarrh is water — and for water-foam catarrh there is no remedy at all (105b:12).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Blow the foam off',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'Head pains.', text: 'Blowing off the foam is bad for head pains (105b:11). You saved your throat and spent your skull.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Skim it off with your hand',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'purse', title: 'Bad for poverty.', text: 'Removing the foam by hand is bad for poverty (105b:11). The patient thing in the corner smiles.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Sink the foam into the drink, then drink',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'The one safe move.', text: '"What is its remedy? He should sink it in and then drink" (105b:11). Throat, skull, and purse all intact.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'the greens',
        title: 'The gardener’s bundle of vegetables sits tied with its cord. One leaf has fallen to the table.',
        he: 'יַרְקָא מִכִּישָׁא דְּאָסַר גִּינָּאָה',
        body: 'People do not eat vegetables straight from the bundle the gardener tied, and they do not eat a vegetable that fell on the table. Abaye had a polite explanation for each. The matron on Rav Ḥisda’s boat had a better one.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:13–15',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.13',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Not eating from the gardener’s tied bundle', first: 'it looks like gluttony — too greedy to untie it', master: 'it is bad for witchcraft', ref: '105b:13' },
          { practice: 'Not eating a vegetable that fell on the table', first: 'it is repulsive', master: 'it is bad for halitosis', ref: '105b:15' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Eat straight from the tied bundle',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'spirit', title: 'You just became reachable.', text: 'The matron who magically pinned Rav Ḥisda and Rabba bar Rav Huna’s boat admitted she was powerless against them — because, among other habits, they never ate from a bundle tied by the gardener (105b:14). You are not so armored.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Untie the bundle first, then eat',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Witchcraft finds no handle.', text: 'The knot is undone and whatever rode in on it is gone. One habit of the sages who could not be cursed at sea (105b:13–14).' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Eat the leaf that fell on the table',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'Bad for halitosis.', text: 'Abaye thought fallen vegetables were merely repulsive; the Master said they are bad for the breath (105b:15). Your dinner companions lean away.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'final waters · mayim acharonim',
        title: 'The meal ends. Before Grace — the final waters.',
        he: 'מַיִם אַחֲרוֹנִים חוֹבָה',
        body: 'Final waters are an obligation, said Rav Yehuda son of Rabbi Ḥiyya, because of Sodomite salt that blinds the eyes — present, said Abaye, a pinch in every kor. The baraita: cold water only, and into a vessel.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105a:15, 17; 105b:2–5',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.4',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Not spilling the final waters on the ground', first: 'it is a matter of messiness', master: 'an evil spirit rests upon them, and passersby are liable to be afflicted', ref: '105b:5' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Cold water, into a vessel',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'The obligation, done properly.', text: 'Cold — because hot water softens the hands and does not remove the dirt (105a:17) — and into a vessel, as the baraita requires for final waters (105a:15). The Sodomite salt goes with the water.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Cold water, poured out on the floor',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'spirit', title: 'Something now rests on that puddle.', text: 'Abaye assumed the rule against ground-spilling was about mess; Rabba told him an evil spirit rests on those waters and passersby can be harmed (105b:5). Your floor is now a hazard for the whole household.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Scalding water your hand recoils from',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'The salt stays.', text: 'For final waters, hot water softens the hands and does not remove the dirt (105a:17) — and Rabbi Yannai bars water the hand recoils from (105b:2). Somewhere on your fingers, a grain of Sodomite salt waits for your eyes.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Skip them — Grace is waiting',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'A pinch in a kor is enough.', text: 'Final waters are an obligation because of Sodomite salt, a small amount of which blinds the eyes (105b:4). Later, rubbing your eye, you remember this moment.' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'night · the courtyard',
        title: 'Porters arrive with your new barrel of wine. Where should they rest it?',
        he: 'לָא יָתְבִי תּוּתֵי מַרְזֵבָא',
        body: 'People do not sit under a gutter. Abaye thought it was about the waste water. In this daf, porters rested a barrel under a gutter — and it burst.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:15–17',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.15',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Not sitting under the gutter', first: 'because of the waste water that pours out', master: 'because demons are commonly found there', ref: '105b:15' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'In the shade under the gutter spout',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'purse', title: 'The barrel bursts.', text: 'When this happened in the daf, Mar bar Rav Ashi blew horns, excommunicated the demon, and made it pay — "these men placed a barrel on my ear," it protested. It paid late: demons have no authority over anything tied, sealed, measured, or counted, so it struggled to find loose money (105b:16–17). No sage is here tonight to collect for you.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'In the middle of the open courtyard',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'Nothing under it but ground.', text: 'Demons frequent the gutter’s shadow, not the open yard (105b:15). The wine survives the night. Mar bar Rav Ashi’s scolding of the demon even held that public places belong to people — it was the one who deviated (105b:17).' },
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        kicker: 'last drink',
        title: 'One more drink of water before sleep. The pitcher waits.',
        he: 'שָׁדֵי מַיָּא מִפּוּמָּא דְּחַצְבָּא',
        body: 'People pour a little water out of the mouth of a pitcher before drinking. Abaye assumed it was about stray twigs. Rav Pappa’s house had a servant — the son of a demon — who knew better, and once came back late from the river because of it.',
        ref: 'Chullin 105b:18–19',
        url: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.105b.18',
        reveal: [
          { practice: 'Pouring a splash from the pitcher’s mouth before drinking', first: 'because of twigs it might contain', master: 'because there are foul waters there', ref: '105b:18' },
        ],
        choices: [
          {
            label: 'Pour off the first splash, then drink',
            outcome: { tone: 'good', meter: null, title: 'The foul waters pass you by.', text: 'Rav Pappa’s demon-born servant delayed at the river and explained: "I waited until the foul waters passed" (105b:19). What a demon waits out, you just poured out.' },
          },
          {
            label: 'Drink straight from the pitcher’s mouth',
            outcome: { tone: 'bad', meter: 'body', title: 'You drank what the demon waited out.', text: 'The Master’s reason was never twigs: there are foul waters at the pitcher’s mouth (105b:18). Even Rav Pappa’s demon servant would not draw until they passed (105b:19).' },
          },
        ],
      },
    ];

    // ---------- rendering ----------
    const $game = document.getElementById('game');
    const $meters = document.getElementById('meters');
    const $masterCount = document.getElementById('master-count');

    function renderMeters() {
      $meters.innerHTML = METERS.map((m) => {
        const val = state[m.key];
        const pips = [0, 1, 2]
          .map((i) => `<span class="pip inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full ${i < val ? '' : 'lost'}" style="background:${m.color}"></span>`)
          .join(' ');
        return `<div class="rounded-xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#140e08] px-2 py-2">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest !text-[#a78d68]">${m.icon} ${m.label}</p>
          <p class="frank text-sm !text-[#ecdfc6]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${m.he}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 space-x-1">${pips}</p>
        </div>`;
      }).join('');
      $masterCount.textContent = String(state.masterSeen.size);
    }

    const TONE = {
      good: { border: '#9dbb7e', label: 'the daf approves', labelColor: '#9dbb7e' },
      bad: { border: '#d4674c', label: 'the daf warned you', labelColor: '#d4674c' },
      warn: { border: '#d9b23f', label: 'permitted, but poorly chosen', labelColor: '#d9b23f' },
      machloket: { border: '#a893d1', label: 'a machloket — two versions', labelColor: '#a893d1' },
    };

    function revealCardHTML(scene) {
      if (!scene.reveal) return '';
      const rows = scene.reveal
        .map(
          (r) => `
          <div class="border-t border-[#3d2c1a] pt-2 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0">
            <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest !text-[#a78d68]">${r.practice} · ${r.ref}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#cbb894]"><span class="frank font-bold !text-[#ecdfc6]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מֵרֵישׁ הֲוָה אָמֵינָא</span> — at first I would say: ${r.first}.</p>
          </div>`
        )
        .join('');
      const backRows = scene.reveal
        .map(
          (r) => `
          <div class="border-t border-[#4a3763] pt-2 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0">
            <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest !text-[#a893d1]">${r.practice} · ${r.ref}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#d9cfec]"><span class="frank font-bold !text-[#e6d9ff]" dir="rtl" lang="he">אָמַר לִי מָר</span> — but the Master said to me: ${r.master}.</p>
          </div>`
        )
        .join('');
      return `
        <div class="flip-wrap mt-4" data-flip>
          <div class="flip-inner">
            <button type="button" data-flip-btn class="flip-face block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#140e08] p-4 text-left hover:border-[#e6a94f]/50 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#e6a94f]">
              <p class="mb-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#e6a94f]">abaye’s first thought — tap to hear the master</p>
              ${rows}
            </button>
            <button type="button" data-flip-btn class="flip-back flip-face block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#6d59a3] bg-[#1c1428] p-4 text-left focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#a893d1]">
              <p class="mb-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#a893d1]">what rabba, the master, revealed</p>
              ${backRows}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>`;
    }

    function renderScene() {
      const i = state.scene;
      if (i >= SCENES.length) return renderEnding();
      const s = SCENES[i];
      $game.innerHTML = `
        <div class="scene-enter rounded-2xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#1e1610] p-5">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#e6a94f]">scene ${i + 1} of ${SCENES.length} · ${s.kicker}</p>
          <h2 class="frank mt-2 text-xl font-bold !text-[#ecdfc6]">${s.title}</h2>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-lg !text-[#e6a94f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${s.he}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cbb894]">${s.body}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] !text-[#7a6749]"><a class="underline hover:!text-[#e6a94f]" href="${s.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${s.ref}</a></p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-2" id="choices">
            ${s.choices
              .map(
                (c, ci) => `
              <button type="button" data-choice="${ci}" class="rounded-xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#140e08] px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm !text-[#ecdfc6] transition hover:border-[#e6a94f]/60 hover:bg-[#241809] focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#e6a94f]">
                ${c.label}
              </button>`
              )
              .join('')}
          </div>
          <div id="outcome"></div>
        </div>`;
      $game.querySelectorAll('[data-choice]').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => choose(Number(btn.dataset.choice)));
      });
    }

    function choose(ci) {
      const s = SCENES[state.scene];
      const c = s.choices[ci];
      const o = c.outcome;
      if (o.meter) state[o.meter] = Math.max(0, state[o.meter] - 1);
      if (o.chasidut) state.chasidut += 1;
      state.log.push({ scene: s.title, choice: c.label, tone: o.tone });
      renderMeters();

      const tone = TONE[o.tone];
      const meterNote = o.meter
        ? `<p class="mt-2 text-[11px] font-bold" style="color:${METERS.find((m) => m.key === o.meter).color}">−1 ${METERS.find((m) => m.key === o.meter).label}</p>`
        : o.chasidut
          ? '<p class="mt-2 text-[11px] font-bold !text-[#9dbb7e]">midat chasidut — remembered for the ending</p>'
          : '';

      const $choices = document.getElementById('choices');
      $choices.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b, bi) => {
        b.disabled = true;
        b.classList.add('opacity-40');
        if (bi === ci) {
          b.classList.remove('opacity-40');
          b.style.borderColor = tone.border;
        }
      });

      document.getElementById('outcome').innerHTML = `
        <div class="scene-enter mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4" style="border-color:${tone.border};background:#140e08">
          <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em]" style="color:${tone.labelColor}">${tone.label}</p>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-base font-bold !text-[#ecdfc6]">${o.title}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#cbb894]">${o.text}</p>
          ${meterNote}
        </div>
        ${revealCardHTML(s)}
        <button type="button" id="next" class="mt-4 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#e6a94f]/50 bg-[#e6a94f]/10 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e6a94f] hover:bg-[#e6a94f]/20 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#e6a94f]">
          ${state.scene + 1 < SCENES.length ? 'The evening continues →' : 'See how the night ends →'}
        </button>`;

      const flipWrap = document.getElementById('outcome').querySelector('[data-flip]');
      if (flipWrap) {
        flipWrap.querySelectorAll('[data-flip-btn]').forEach((b) =>
          b.addEventListener('click', () => {
            flipWrap.classList.toggle('flipped');
            if (flipWrap.classList.contains('flipped')) {
              (SCENES[state.scene].reveal || []).forEach((r) => state.masterSeen.add(r.ref + r.practice));
              renderMeters();
            }
          })
        );
      }
      document.getElementById('next').addEventListener('click', () => {
        state.scene += 1;
        renderScene();
        $game.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      });
      document.getElementById('next').focus({ preventScroll: true });
    }

    function renderEnding() {
      const total = state.body + state.purse + state.spirit;
      let title, he, text;
      if (total === 9 && state.chasidut >= 2) {
        title = 'Wine, son of wine';
        he = 'חַמְרָא בַּר חַמְרָא';
        text = 'Every meter intact, and the stricter path taken twice. Mar Ukva measured himself against his father and came up "vinegar, son of wine" (105a:9) — tonight you would not have to. The angel of poverty passes your window without slowing.';
      } else if (total >= 8) {
        title = 'Vinegar, son of wine';
        he = 'חַלָּא בַּר חַמְרָא';
        text = 'Mar Ukva’s own grade for himself: sound practice, a notch below the household’s best (105a:9). You end the evening whole — one habit short of your father’s table.';
      } else if (total >= 5) {
        title = 'The asteira slips away';
        he = 'אִיסְתֵּירָא';
        text = 'You reach your bed, but the evening collected its tolls. Rav Asi patrolled daily and wondered where Shmuel’s promised coins were — until the night the channel burst showed him every coin at once (105a:12). Tonight, some of yours washed downstream.';
      } else {
        title = 'The angel makes itself at home';
        he = 'שָׂרָא דְּעַנְיוּתָא';
        text = 'Foam drunk, crumbs scattered, waters spilled where spirits rest. The man in the daf kept the angel of poverty out of his house for years through nothing but care at the table (105b:10). Tonight, the angel found your door open.';
      }
      const lost = [];
      METERS.forEach((m) => {
        const l = 3 - state[m.key];
        if (l > 0) lost.push(`${m.icon} ${m.label}: −${l}`);
      });
      $game.innerHTML = `
        <div class="scene-enter rounded-2xl border border-[#e6a94f]/40 bg-[#1e1610] p-6 text-center">
          <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#e6a94f]">the evening ends</p>
          <h2 class="frank mt-2 text-3xl font-black !text-[#ecdfc6]">${title}</h2>
          <p class="frank mt-1 text-2xl !text-[#e6a94f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${he}</p>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-md text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#cbb894]">${text}</p>
          <div class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xs rounded-xl border border-[#3d2c1a] bg-[#140e08] p-3 text-xs !text-[#a78d68]">
            <p>meters kept: <b class="!text-[#ecdfc6]">${total} / 9</b>${lost.length ? ' · ' + lost.join(' · ') : ' · nothing lost'}</p>
            <p class="mt-1">midat chasidut: <b class="!text-[#9dbb7e]">${state.chasidut}</b> · the master’s reasons heard: <b class="!text-[#e6a94f]">${state.masterSeen.size} / 8</b></p>
          </div>
          ${
            state.masterSeen.size < 8
              ? '<p class="mt-3 text-[11px] !text-[#a893d1]">Some of the Master’s hidden reasons went unheard — replay and flip every card.</p>'
              : '<p class="mt-3 text-[11px] !text-[#a893d1]">All eight of the Master’s reasons heard. Abaye himself needed Rabba to tell him.</p>'
          }
          <button type="button" id="replay" class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-[#e6a94f]/50 bg-[#e6a94f]/10 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#e6a94f] hover:bg-[#e6a94f]/20 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#e6a94f]">
            Host the meal again 🕯️
          </button>
        </div>`;
      document.getElementById('replay').addEventListener('click', () => {
        const seen = state.masterSeen;
        state = freshState();
        state.masterSeen = seen;
        renderMeters();
        renderScene();
        $game.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      });
    }

    state = freshState();
    renderMeters();
    renderScene();
  </script>
</Layout>
